  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Consider the function \(f(x) = \frac{6}{x-2}\).</para>
<para>To find out the sets of possible input and output values of the function, Clare created a table and evaluated \(f\) at some values of \(x\). Along the way, she ran into some trouble.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Find \(f(x)\) for each \(x\)-value Clare listed. Describe what Clare’s trouble might be. </item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis></entry><entry>
       -10
      </entry>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(\frac12\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
      2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        8
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>\(f(x)\)</emphasis></entry><entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

